# Line endings are decided here, once, for everyone — not by whatever
# core.autocrlf each machine happens to have.
#
# Why this file exists: two of this repository's gates hash the bytes of a file
# on disk. C1 in scripts/check.js compares spec/architecture.md against
# spec/architecture.sha256, and the AI evaluator compares qa/ai/data/
# eval-cases.jsonl against its manifest. Both recorded hashes are of LF content.
# On Windows with the default core.autocrlf=true, a fresh clone writes CRLF, so
# both hashes miss by the line endings alone: `npm run check` and `npm run
# eval:ai` fail on a clone where nothing is wrong, and `git status` reports
# every text file as modified while `git diff` shows no change at all.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` ends that: git decides what is text, and every text file is
# written to the working tree with LF on every platform. Editors on Windows
# handle LF; the gates and the hashes then mean what they say.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text. Listed by type rather
# than by path so a new screenshot or font needs no change here.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.zip  binary
*.db      binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.sqlite3 binary
